.Sh DESCRIPTION
This command can be used to display the contents (after decryption as
the case may be) fetched from the given URI.
.Sh OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Sy -help
Print out a usage message.
.It Sy -out Em filename
This specifies the output file to write to.
Standard output is used if this option is not present.
The output file can be the same as the input, which leads to replacing
the file contents.
Note that file I/O is not atomic.
The output file is truncated and then written.
.It Sy -noout
this option prevents output of the PEM data.
.It Sy -passin Em arg
the key password source.
For more information about the format of
.Em arg
see
.Xr openssl-passphrase-options 1 .
.It Sy -text
Prints out the objects in text form, similarly to the
.Sy -text
output from
.Xr openssl-x509 1 ,
.Xr openssl-pkey 1 ,
etc.
.It Sy -r
Fetch objects recursively when possible.
.It Sy -certs
.It Sy -keys
.It Sy -crls
Only select the certificates, keys or CRLs from the given URI. However,
if this URI would return a set of names (URIs), those are always
returned.
.Pp
Note that all options must be given before the
.Em uri
argument.
.Pp
Note
.Em -keys
selects exclusively private keys, there is no selector for public keys
only.
.It Sy -subject Em arg
Search for an object having the subject name
.Em arg .
.Pp
The arg must be formatted as
.Qo Li /type0=value0/type1=value1/type2=... Qc .
Special characters may be escaped by
.Qo Li \e Qc
(backslash), whitespace is retained.
Empty values are permitted but are ignored for the search.
That is, a search with an empty value will have the same effect as not
specifying the type at all.
Giving a single
.Qo Li / Qc
will lead to an empty sequence of RDNs (a NULL-DN). Multi-valued RDNs
can be formed by placing a
.Qo Li + Qc
character instead of a
.Qo Li / Qc
between the AttributeValueAssertions (AVAs) that specify the members of
the set.
.Pp
Example:
.Pp
.Qo Li /DC=org/DC=OpenSSL/DC=users/UID=123456+CN=John Doe Qc
.It Sy -issuer Em arg
.It Sy -serial Em arg
Search for an object having the given issuer name and serial number.
These two options
.Em must
be used together.
The issuer arg must be formatted as
.Qo Li /type0=value0/type1=value1/type2=... Qc ,
characters may be escaped by \e (backslash), no spaces are skipped.
The serial arg may be specified as a decimal value or a hex value if
preceded by
.Qo Li 0x Qc .
.It Sy -alias Em arg
Search for an object having the given alias.
.It Sy -fingerprint Em arg
Search for an object having the given fingerprint.
.It Sy - Ns Em digest
The digest that was used to compute the fingerprint given with
.Sy -fingerprint .
.It Sy -engine Em id
See
.Xr openssl 1 .
This option is deprecated.
.It Sy -provider Em name
.It Sy -provider-path Em path
.It Sy -provparam Em [name:]key=value
.It Sy -propquery Em propq
See
.Xr openssl 1 ,
.Xr provider 7 ,
and
.Xr property 7 .
.El
